[1m=== Tutorial: basic_operations ===[0m

[32mLearn basic Olang operations and syntax[0m
[33mDifficulty:[0m Beginner
[33mEstimated Time:[0m 5 minutes

[36mStep 1: Basic Arithmetic[0m
[2mLet's start with simple arithmetic operations[0m

[35mCode to try:[0m
[34m2 + 3 * 4
[0m

[32mExpected Output:[0m
[32m14
[0m

[33mExplanation:[0m
[2mOlang follows standard operator precedence: multiplication before addition[0m

[36mHINTS:[0m
   • [2mUse parentheses to change precedence: (2 + 3) * 4[0m

---

[36mStep 2: Variables[0m
[2mCreating and using variables[0m

[35mCode to try:[0m
[34mlet name = "Alice"
let age = 25
println(name + " is " + age + " years old")
[0m

[32mExpected Output:[0m
[32mAlice is 25 years old
[0m

[33mExplanation:[0m
[2mVariables are created with 'let' and can be reassigned[0m

[36mHINTS:[0m
   • [2mUse to_string() to convert numbers to strings if needed[0m

---

[36mStep 3: Functions[0m
[2mDefining and calling functions[0m

[35mCode to try:[0m
[34mfn greet(name) = "Hello, " + name + "!"
greet("World")
[0m

[32mExpected Output:[0m
[32mHello, World!
[0m

[33mExplanation:[0m
[2mFunctions are defined with 'fn' and can have parameters[0m

[36mHINTS:[0m
   • [2mUse => for multi-line functions: fn name() => { ... }[0m

---

